measurement_GEO_lichnerowicz_statement=(gamma^mu D_mu)^2 Psi = g^{mu nu} nabla_mu D_nu Psi + c R Psi with c = -1/4; R = g^{sn} R^r_{s r n}, R^r_{s m n} = d_m Gamma^r_{ns} - d_n Gamma^r_{ms} + Gamma^r_{ml} Gamma^l_{ns} - Gamma^r_{nl} Gamma^l_{ms}
measurement_GEO_spinCurvature_statement=F_{mu nu} = d_mu Omega_nu - d_nu Omega_mu + [Omega_mu, Omega_nu] = (1/2) R_{ab mu nu} S^{ab}, R_{ab mu nu} = eta_ac e_r^c R^r_{s mu nu} e_b^s
measurement_EMT_signConvention=T_{mu nu} = -(2/sqrt|g|) dS/dg^{mu nu} reproduces CONTRACT section 7 exactly: T^mu_mu(no sum) = (h_mu/sqrt|g|) dL/dh_mu for diagonal e = diag(h); rho = T_44/N^2 = -(N/sqrt|g|) dL/dN; p_i = T^i_i = (h_i/sqrt|g|) dL/dh_i; homogeneous: rho = m S + U, p = L_s (= S U' - U on shell)
measurement_EMT_traceStatement=T^mu_mu = 7 K - 8 (m S + U) off shell; on shell T^mu_mu = -m S + 7 S U' - 8 U (= -m S + 3 lam S^2 for U = lam S^2/2)
measurement_LAG_commutingProxyJustification=Commuting proxy: the Lagrangian is bilinear in (Psibar-jets, Psi-jets) and every term is written with the Psibar factor (Psi^* or d_mu Psi^*) to the LEFT of the Psi factor. The Grassmann left derivative d/dPsi^*_a acts on that leftmost factor without any sign, so term by term it equals the ordinary derivative of the same polynomial in commuting symbols; the EL expression is linear in the Psi-jets, hence evaluating it on commuting exact rationals is exact. (For the Psi-equation the Grassmann result differs from the commuting one only by an overall sign.) The genuine Grassmann computation is repeated in demo_grassmann_lagrangians.py.
